			title: "Naphthalene"
			x: 10.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5ADAD2566FD74648"]
			description: ["Burns naphthalene over vanadium pentoxide in air into &6phthalic anhydride&r. It takes 480 EU/t now, so it needs HV power. Naphthalene, air and small vanadium pentoxide dust, in a chemical reactor on an HV hatch. 2-ethylanthraquinone in the chemical plant. Naphthalene and air by pipe, vanadium dust by bus, the anhydride out by bus to the plant."]
			icon: "gtceu:phthalic_anhydride_dust"
			id: "5D511A6DD8DA757A"
			rewards: [{ id: "37121CFEAAEC9AF5", type: "xp", xp: 35 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 15L, id: "186016EC2C83A578", item: "gtceu:phthalic_anhydride_dust", type: "item" }]
			title: "Phthalic Anhydride"
			x: 12.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5D511A6DD8DA757A"]
			description: ["Joins phthalic anhydride and ethylbenzene into &62-ethylanthraquinone&r in GT--'s chemical plant.       At HV build it from aluminium frostproof plant casings, HV machine casings, steel pipe casings and cupronickel coils. Only the machine casings set the recipe tier: a lower tier sits idle with no error, while pipes and coils can stay low tier. The preview draws titanium pipes and nichrome coils, which are EV and not needed here. The chemical plant as above, phthalic anhydride and ethylbenzene from the coal gas distillery. The hydrogenation step. The EAQ then circulates and is never used up. Anhydride by bus, ethylbenzene by pipe, the EAQ on to the hydrogenation hatch."]
			icon: "gtnn:exxonmobil_chemical_plant"
			id: "31DFB4094256A533"
			rewards: [{ id: "77CC09A91047DA64", type: "xp", xp: 45 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "3253FB0AE1D62B75", item: "gtnn:exxonmobil_chemical_plant", type: "item" }]
			title: "2-Ethylanthraquinone"
			x: 14.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["31DFB4094256A533"]
			description: ["Adds hydrogen to EAQ over a palladium-vanadium catalyst: &6EAHQ&r, the carrier that holds the hydrogen for the peroxide. EAQ, hydrogen from the syngas plant, and the catalyst built from the MV platline's palladium. Hydrogen peroxide. Hydrogen by pipe from the syngas plant, the catalyst by bus; the EAQ comes back round the loop."]
			icon: "gtceu:ethyl_anthra_hydro_quinone_bucket"
			id: "1DCB925CCCB2B473"
			rewards: [{ id: "7033C130AE2785E8", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "3A463F34C4A3E00B", item: "gtceu:ethyl_anthra_hydro_quinone_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hydrogenation to EAHQ"
			x: 16.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1DCB925CCCB2B473"]
			description: ["Air oxidizes EAHQ back to EAQ and releases &6hydrogen peroxide&r. This is the only route: the direct hydrogen and oxygen reactors are gone. EAHQ and air in the chemical plant, whose machine casings must be HV (480 EU/t), plus a little anthracene to make up losses. Hydrazine. The EAQ it returns goes back into the hydrogenation. Close the loop: EAQ back by pipe, peroxide on to the hydrazine step, anthracene by bus."]
			icon: "gtceu:hydrogen_peroxide_bucket"
			id: "7DF6770260AAEE58"
			rewards: [{ id: "5C026F2B9BF10620", type: "xp", xp: 45 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "50017F83A611C5A4", item: "gtceu:hydrogen_peroxide_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hydrogen Peroxide"
			x: 18.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DF6770260AAEE58"]
			description: ["Ammonia and peroxide make &6hydrazine&r by the peroxide process. Ammonia, hydrogen peroxide and the chemical plant on HV machine casings (480 EU/t). Aerozine 50. Ammonia from the coke-oven or Haber line by pipe, hydrazine on to the mixer."]
			icon: "gtceu:hydrazine_bucket"
			id: "140DA37B98D4C09F"
